Body:
@rekram1-node I noticed the failed E2E test and tried to fix it. I realized when merging the metadata of the detected models and models from Models.dev or config file, `api.npm` is overriden to `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`. This will cause issues (e.g. `opencode/gpt-5-nano` needs `@ai-sdk/openai` instead). I've fixed it.

However, the E2E test still fails after that. According to the error message, it seems that the model detection populates a lot more new models under the `opencode` provider, in the test the app tries to use "gemini-3-pro" to generate the session title, and is thus denied. I don't have a good idea about how to fix it. I simply skip the model detection for `opencode` provider, and the E2E test is now able to pass locally. Could you re-trigger the test here?

Given that Models.dev are maintained by you as well, ig it's okay?

For quick workaround create file `.opencode/plugin/safety.ts` with following code:

```
import { type Hooks, type PluginInput } from "./index"

const MAX_FILE_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024 // 10MB

export default function SafetyPlugin(input: PluginInput): Hooks {
  return {
    "tool.execute.before": ({ tool }, { args }) => {
      if (tool !== "read") return

      const { filePath } = args as { filePath: string }

      // Skip non-existent files - delegate to read tool's error handling
      const size = Bun.file(filePath).size
      if (size === 0) return

      if (size > MAX_FILE_SIZE) {
        const sizeMB = (size / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(2)
        throw new Error(`File too large: ${filePath} (${sizeMB}MB exceeds ${MAX_FILE_SIZE / 1024 / 1024}MB limit)`)
      }
    },
  }
}
```
